W: 1. How should I your true love know
W: From another one?
W: By his cockle hat and staff
W: And his sandal shoon.
W:
W: 2. He is dead and gone, lady,
W: He is dead and gone;
W: At his head a grass-green turf
W: At his heels a stone.
W:
W: 3. White his shroud as the mountain snow,
W: Larded with sweet flowers.
W: Which bewept to the grave did not go
W: With true-love showers.
